# 2️⃣ Units — Very Important 🚨

Common units:

```text id="1q1n8a"
km/h
m/s
```

Conversion:

[
\boxed{1\ km/h=\frac{5}{18}\ m/s}
]

Therefore:

[
\boxed{1\ m/s=\frac{18}{5}\ km/h}
]

### Example

Convert:

[
72\ km/h
]

to m/s:

[
72\times\frac5{18}
]

[
\boxed{20\ m/s}
]

---

# 3️⃣ Fast Conversion Trick

### km/h → m/s

Multiply by:

[
\boxed{\frac5{18}}
]

### m/s → km/h

Multiply by:

[
\boxed{\frac{18}{5}}
]

Examples:

[
54\ km/h=54\times5/18=\boxed{15m/s}
]

[
25m/s=25\times18/5=\boxed{90km/h}
]

