# 5️⃣ Average Speed ⭐

Average speed is:

[
\boxed{
\frac{Total\ Distance}{Total\ Time}
}
]

⚠️ Don't automatically take the arithmetic average of speeds.

---

# 6️⃣ Equal-Distance Shortcut

If equal distances are travelled at speeds (a) and (b):

[
\boxed{
Average\ Speed=\frac{2ab}{a+b}
}
]

Example:

Equal distances at:

[
40,\ 60\ km/h
]

[
Average=\frac{2(40)(60)}{40+60}
]

[
=\boxed{48\ km/h}
]

---

# 7️⃣ Equal-Time Shortcut

If equal time is spent at speeds (a) and (b):

[
\boxed{
Average=\frac{a+b}{2}
}
]

Example:

Equal time at:

[
40,\ 60
]

Average:

[
\boxed{50\ km/h}
]

---

# 🔥 8️⃣ Relative Speed

Relative speed tells us:

> How quickly one object approaches or moves away from another.

---

## Objects Moving in Opposite Directions

Add speeds:

[
\boxed{Relative\ Speed=S_1+S_2}
]

Example:

```text id="m5ddqa"
A →→→       ←←← B
  40 km/h   60 km/h
```

Relative speed:

[
40+60
]

[
\boxed{100\ km/h}
]

---

# 9️⃣ Objects Moving in Same Direction

Subtract speeds:

[
\boxed{Relative\ Speed=|S_1-S_2|}
]

Example:

```text id="hbr0gt"
A →→→→
B   →→
```

Speeds:

[
70,\ 50
]

Relative speed:

[
70-50
]

[
\boxed{20\ km/h}
]

